From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(interaction): forward Bedrock fluid pickup

Java empty buckets send use-in-air, but Bedrock fluid pickup requires the
source-fluid block hit. Route empty main-hand bucket use through the normal
block-use path on direct and negotiated ViaProxy Bedrock sessions. Preserve
Java reach, source-fluid ray tracing, occlusion, selected-slot synchronization
and prediction sequencing.

Target evidence is the Java 26.3 BucketItem implementation and Geyser's
BedrockInventoryTransactionTranslator source-fluid bucket handling. Tests
exercise water and lava targets, flowing fluid rejection, reach and solid
occlusion. Ordinary Java sessions retain their existing behavior.
